The '''Treaty of Arktici''' is a multilateral agreement signed on December 1, 1963, in XXX. It establishes the legal framework for the use and governance of Arktici, ensuring that the region is used exclusively for peaceful purposes and international scientific cooperation. The original signatories of the treaty include the governments of Balisca, XXX, XXX, XXX, XXX, XXX, XXX, XXX, XXX, and XXX. 


== Key Provisions ==
The treaty applies to all areas north of the 60° North latitude, including all ice shelves. Its primary articles outline the following agreements:
* '''Peaceful Use (Article I & V):''' Arktici is strictly reserved for peaceful purposes. The establishment of military bases, fortifications, military maneuvers, and weapons testing are entirely prohibited. Furthermore, any nuclear tests or disposal of radioactive waste material are banned. Military personnel and equipment may only be used for scientific research or other peaceful applications.
* '''Scientific Cooperation (Article II & III):''' Freedom of scientific investigation shall continue as applied during 1963. Contracting parties agree to exchange information on scientific programs, freely share scientific observations and results, and exchange scientific personnel between stations and expeditions.
* '''Territorial Claims (Article IV):''' The treaty freezes territorial claims. It does not require any contracting party to renounce their previously asserted rights or claims to territorial sovereignty in Arktici. However, no activities taking place while the treaty is in force can constitute a basis for asserting, supporting, or denying a claim, and no new claims or enlargements of existing claims can be asserted.
* '''Observation and Inspection (Article VII):''' Designated observers have complete freedom of access at any time to all areas of Arktici, including stations, installations, equipment, ships, and aircraft. Aerial observations are also permitted.
* '''Jurisdiction (Article VIII):''' Observers and scientific personnel remain under the jurisdiction of their own contracting party's agencies (such as the USNW, East Althenian Sphere, or Alcadean Union) regarding any acts or omissions occurring while exercising their functions in Arktici.
* '''Administration and Dispute Resolution (Article IX & XI):''' Representatives of the contracting parties are to meet periodically in XXX to exchange information and formulate measures to further the treaty's objectives. Disputes regarding interpretation or application should be resolved through peaceful means, and may be referred to the International Court of Justice with the consent of all parties involved.
* '''Languages and Depositary (Article XIII & XIV):''' The treaty is deposited with the Government of Balisca. The authentic texts are recorded in the Trent, XXX, XXX, and XXX languages.

== Territorial Claims ==
Prior to the treaty, several nations had established territorial claims in Arktici based on historical exploration.

* '''XXX:''' Claims Marie-Elise Land, stretching from 180°W to 160°W. This territory was claimed in 1875 and formally recognized in 1924, based on explorations by XXX explorer Victor D'Aberville.
* '''XXX:''' Claims the XXX Arktician Territory , comprising the region between 160°W and 125°W. It was claimed in 1933.
* '''XXX:''' Claims Arkticia (Territorio XXX Arkticio), from 125°W to 78°W. It was created on July 11, 1961.
* '''XXX:''' Claims the XXX Arktician Territory between 90°W and 30°W. The territory was officially formed on March 3, 1962, though claims date back to 1908 and 1917.
* '''Balisca:''' Claims [[Baliscan Arktici]], delimited by the 80°W and 40°W meridians. The claim was established in 1904.
* '''XXX:''' Claims XXX Arkticia from 30°W to 50°E, making it the largest claim in Arktici. It was formalized in 1932 following explorations in 1939.
* '''XXX:''' Claims XXX Land, located between 50°E and 125°E. Formalized in 1894 and named after Queen Kristina, the claim is based on multiple Merveigian explorations.
* '''XXX:''' Claims the XXX Arktician Dependency, from 165°E to 180°E. The claim was formalized in 1923.


